  "texts": {
    "preamble": "K.S.R.Natarajan vs The Food Inspector on 30 June, 2017 Author: N.Sathish Kumar Bench: N.Sathish Kumar In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 30.06.2017 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice N.Sathish Kumar Crl.R.C. No.361 of 2011 1. K.S.R.Natarajan 2. N.Senthilnathan 3.",
    "facts": "The brief facts of the prosecution case is that the respondent has filed a complaint as against the revision petitioners under Sections 7(ii) and 16(1)(a)(i) r/w. Section 2(ix) (k) of the P.F.A. Act 1954 and Rule 32(e) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act Rule 1955. Since the complaint was filed otherwise than a police report, necessary witnesses have been examined. At this stage, the petitioners have filed a petition to discharge them from the said complaint.",
    "arguments": "3. The main contention of the petitioners is that there is a delay in lodging the complaint and also in obtaining sanction and also getting opinion of the expert.",
